      ":question/id": "d03c1a97-b5ab-5f7f-8617-41aa11bd19ff",
      ":question/problem": "Find the shortest distance between the point $(15,-3)$ and the line $y=6.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](images/61/61922e0beb73c0968939c50f1c317e889572ac771ef752079a40eff5709f8a26.png)\n\nSince the line $y=6$ is a horizontal line, the shortest distance between this line and the point $(15,-3)$ is given by the absolute value of the difference between $y$-coordinate of the point and $6.$ \n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=|-3-6|=9.\n$$",
